ct-paging.patch — applied by .github/workflows/rekor-monitor.yml to
sigstore/rekor-monitor at the pinned commit before `go build`, with
`git apply --check` first, so a change upstream to either hunk fails
the step by name instead of applying fuzzily (#1237).

What upstream does (2cbcfa26, and main fbc5fc4, 2026-11-13):
GetCTLogEntries calls ctclient.GetEntries(start, end) once.
certificate-transparency-go sends one get-entries request and does not
page, and ctfe.sigstore.dev caps a response by size (604 of 2,001 and
900 of 4,901 requested, measured 2026-11-15). The monitor then writes
its checkpoint at the log head, so everything past the first page is
never read, and the run is green. Measured on a real signer
certificate at CT index 443,908,396: found in 443908300..443908500,
missed with exit 0 in 443907396..443909396.

What this patch changes:
1. GetCTLogEntries loops get-entries from start to end, advancing by
   the number of entries each response actually returned. A response
   with no entries before the end is an error, never a loop.
2. It prints one line, `ct-monitor-read: count=N start=S end=E`, which
   the workflow checks against the range between the old checkpoint
   and the new one: the monitor cannot advance its checkpoint over
   certificates it did not read.
3. The RFC 6962 end index is tree_size - 1, the last entry the signed
   tree head covers. Upstream passes tree_size, one past it; that
   entry exists only if the log has grown since the head was read,
   and get-entries answers 400 for an index beyond the log.

Remove this patch, and its apply step, when the pinned rekor-monitor
pages get-entries by itself.

diff --git a/cmd/ct_monitor/main.go b/cmd/ct_monitor/main.go
index 1d0caf9..d9eade1 100644
--- a/cmd/ct_monitor/main.go
+++ b/cmd/ct_monitor/main.go
@@ -121,7 +121,7 @@ func (l CTMonitorLogic) GetStartIndex(prev cmd.Checkpoint, _ cmd.LogInfo) *int64
 
 func (l CTMonitorLogic) GetEndIndex(cur cmd.LogInfo) *int64 {
 	currentSTH := cur.(*ctgo.SignedTreeHead)
-	checkpointEndIndex := int64(currentSTH.TreeSize) //nolint: gosec // G115
+	checkpointEndIndex := int64(currentSTH.TreeSize) - 1 //nolint: gosec // G115
 	return &checkpointEndIndex
 }
 
diff --git a/pkg/ct/v1/monitor.go b/pkg/ct/v1/monitor.go
index 63c33db..eaac2cb 100644
--- a/pkg/ct/v1/monitor.go
+++ b/pkg/ct/v1/monitor.go
@@ -27,10 +27,19 @@ import (
 )
 
 func GetCTLogEntries(ctx context.Context, logClient *ctclient.LogClient, startIndex int64, endIndex int64) ([]ct.LogEntry, error) {
-	entries, err := logClient.GetEntries(ctx, startIndex, endIndex)
-	if err != nil {
-		return nil, fmt.Errorf("error retrieving certificate transparency log entries: %v", err)
+	var entries []ct.LogEntry
+	for next := startIndex; next <= endIndex; {
+		page, err := logClient.GetEntries(ctx, next, endIndex)
+		if err != nil {
+			return nil, fmt.Errorf("error retrieving certificate transparency log entries: %v", err)
+		}
+		if len(page) == 0 {
+			return nil, fmt.Errorf("zero-progress page: no entries at index %d of range %d..%d", next, startIndex, endIndex)
+		}
+		entries = append(entries, page...)
+		next += int64(len(page))
 	}
+	fmt.Fprintf(os.Stderr, "ct-monitor-read: count=%d start=%d end=%d\n", len(entries), startIndex, endIndex)
 	return entries, nil
 }
 
